+# DOT accession records for senior staff briefings and FAA follow-up
+
+Public derivative of the November 9, 2026 Eastern source review · B129 / PD03–PD05
+
+The original NARA accession workbook supplies an exact **Deputy Secretary appointment-file accession covering August 31 and December 12, 2006**. Separate Peters appointment and travel accessions begin after the August referral date and cover December 12. These are dated container-level leads for the senior staff and briefing trail identified in former DOT Inspector General Kenneth Mead's testimony. Their indexes and contents remain unacquired. [NARA FY 2023 workbook, Sheet1 rows 807, 813 and 815](https://www.archives.gov/files/new-accessions/fy-23-accessions.xls) · [Mead's statement, physical p. 71](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-110hhrg41854/pdf/CHRG-110hhrg41854.pdf#page=71)
+
+## What the accession records show
+
+| Locator | Exact accession and relevant boundaries |
+| --- | --- |
+| **FY 2023 Sheet1 row 813** | **TR-0398-2021-0015**, five containers, tabular **April 12, 2005–December 18, 2007**. The title reads **Deputy Secretariat Maria Cino's Appointments (April 12, 2005 - December 18, 2007)**. The span covers both the August referral report and December investigation closure dates. |
+| **FY 2023 rows 815 and 807** | **TR-0398-2021-0012**, four containers of Secretary Mary Peters appointments, **October 4, 2006–October 30, 2008**. **TR-0398-2021-0009**, four containers, tabular **October 13, 2006–January 10, 2009**. Its title reads **Secretary Mary Peter's Travel Records (2006-2009)**. The tabular dates overlap the December closure date. Keep the title, dates and distinct series labels with each record. |
+| **FY 2023 rows 812 and 808** | The two additional Peters appointment accessions **TR-0398-2022-0004** and **TR-0398-2022-0002** begin **January 3, 2007** and **March 1, 2007**, respectively. Their tabular spans both include **March 31, 2007** and **October 2, 2007**, the reporting-period end and House referral date for communication 3550. The date overlap supplies a later search window. |
+| **FY 2023 row 811** | **TR-0398-2022-0008**, one container. The title gives **February 8, 2001 - November 8, 2005**. The original typed date cells are **44235** and **44508** in the workbook's date system, which decode to **February 8, 2021–November 8, 2021**. The HTML register displays **2/8/2021** and **11/8/2021**. The title-versus-date discrepancy therefore also appears in the workbook. The corrected date metadata and actual folder coverage remain open. |
+| **FY 2019 Q3 notice, RG 398** | **LTI-0398-2019-0003**, 11 unrestricted containers of Mineta and Peters appointment files, **June 11, 2002–November 30, 2006**. The notice separately lists **LTI-0398-2019-0001**, one unrestricted container of **Committee Files**, **October 1, 1986–December 31, 2003**. The committee-file span covers the original answer date. It ends before the 2006 follow-up. The notice gives no committee names or folder inventory. [FY 2019 Q3 notice](https://www.archives.gov/research/accessions/2019-quarter-3#:~:text=LTI-0398-2019-0001) |
+
+The FY 2023 rows above identify the Textual Records Division at College Park and have blank FRC Transfer Number cells. This does not determine whether an agency transfer number or earlier custody exists. These dates describe accession records. The August 31 report date, October 17 Secretary swearing-in ceremony and December 12 investigation closure are separate event fields. The transfer records could hold agendas, briefing material or other appointment documentation. Their scope needs to be tested against the case number or subject in an actual folder. [NARA register](https://www.archives.gov/research/accessions) · [August referral report](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=1) · [October ceremony](https://georgewbush-whitehouse.archives.gov/news/releases/2006/10/20061017-7.html) · [Earlier closure study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/CONFLICTS.md)
+
+## Briefings, calendars, invitations and committee minutes
+
+- **Briefing books.** DAA-0398-2024-0005 item **0001** describes appointment, travel and subject briefing books including schedules, agendas and topics of discussion. Some briefing material can be filed apart from the calendar entry. The item is permanent and lists a planned initial span of **2001–2009**. The first page refers calendars to the DOT Capstone authority and correspondence to a separate schedule. The different series descriptions leave the actual calendar, meeting packet and dispatch independently searchable. The approved span does not match an accession to this item. [Current schedule, physical pp. 1, 4–5](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0398/daa-0398-2024-0005_sf115.pdf#page=4)
+- **Invitations.** Item **0002** separately describes accepted and declined invitations and gives a temporary seven-year instruction after cutoff. It is a different file class. Whether a particular 2006 internal meeting generated any such file or came under that authority is open. [Current schedule, physical p. 5](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0398/daa-0398-2024-0005_sf115.pdf#page=5)
+- **Older official committee records.** NC1-398-80-01 physical p. 5 has an amended item **7**. Typed **7/a(2)** describes records about establishment, organization, membership and policy of internal committees and gives a two-year instruction after committee termination. Handwritten **7/b(1)** separately describes agendas, minutes, final reports and related records documenting DOT-sponsored official boards or committees. It provides permanent disposition for the record copy, temporary instructions for other copies, and distinct treatment for other committee records. The NARA cover dated **06/10/2026** displays **7/A/1** and **7/B/1/A** as **P(Active)** and **7/A/2**, **7/B/1/B** and **7/B/2** as **T(Active)**. The current briefing schedule explicitly names older items **5** and **6**. These texts leave the 2006 senior staff meetings' status as a sponsored board or committee and any disposition under item 7 unresolved. The crossed-out original item 7/b language and handwritten replacement both remain visible on the preserved scan. [Historical schedule, cover and physical p. 5](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0398/nc1-398-80-01_sf115.pdf#page=5)
+- **Secretarial reports.** Historical item **3**, **REPORTS (SPECIAL)**, describes biweekly highlight reports and similar Secretarial-level reports. This supplies a separate title to look for in inventories or original issue files. It leaves the relationship to the Mineta **Reports** accession and any 2006 briefing unsettled. [Historical schedule, physical p. 4](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0398/nc1-398-80-01_sf115.pdf#page=4)
+
+## Verification and open inputs
+
+Read **11,638 data rows** across three public workbooks. The stated RG/ID rule returned 15 records, all in FY 2023 **Sheet1 rows 801–815**, with no duplicate accession ID in that set. For all 15, the HTML's displayed text fields and date values matched the independently parsed spreadsheet fields after the stated display and date conversions. The ledger preserves raw date serials, workbook row and cell fields, and HTML accession-line locators. NARA describes the data as supplied by transferring agencies and subject to archival revision. The workbook and HTML are two representations of that data. [FY 2021 workbook](https://www.archives.gov/files/new-accessions/fy-21-accessions.xls) · [FY 2022 workbook](https://www.archives.gov/files/new-accessions/fy-22-accessions.xls) · [FY 2023 workbook](https://www.archives.gov/files/new-accessions/fy-23-accessions.xls) · [Verification ledger](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+- [ ] **PD03–PD05.** Locate the folder/box list and originating accession paperwork for the Cino and Peters appointments. Seek any dated agenda, briefing, OIG action item or written decision keyed to **CC-2006-085 / 042R0122001**. Check the historical committee and briefing filing routes independently and retain actual series/item classifications if found.
+- [ ] **PD01 / PD07.** The 2003 committee-file span is a locator only. Acquire a folder list and scope before connecting it to the May 2003 question, or to any correction.
+- [ ] **PD01–PD03.** The corrected answer and dated receipt, signed action/no-action decision, case-keyed recommendation dispositions and House 3550 cover/enclosure remain open. Preserve each as a separate event or missing record.
